{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"STATUS UPDATE — BOTH FIXES ARE MERGED; THIS STORY NOW WAITS ONLY ON ONE HARNESS VERDICT.\n\nMERGED to main (verified present on origin/main and gerrit/main at bd3de0f864, content checked rather\nthan assumed):\n  * c83263b7d4 — Gerrit 1231, this story's diagnosis + RED-first tests\n  * ff7a761267 — Gerrit 1232, the 8d68 product fix (inbound_differ forwards the canonical identity;\n    apply_inbound_records keys the mint on it)\nThe operator overrode the repo-wide pip-audit block that had been holding the whole stack; another\nsession separately fixed its cause (see e47e-a33d-b9cf-4421 / Gerrit 1239).\n\nTHE ONE REMAINING ITEM: harness run 30772461871, dispatched against main @ bd3de0f864 — the first\ntree containing d067's status-transition fix AND the 8d68 mint fix AND this story's oracle rewrite.\nTwo cells decide this story:\n  * test_outbound_mutation_round_trips[04-transition-status] — already green on the two previous\n    runs (30765232591, 30767546938), so this is a re-confirmation rather than an open question.\n  * test_the_inbound_assignee_mints_a_jira_family_identity — failed on run 30767546938 with\n    \"THE PASS MINTED NOTHING\", which is what led to filing 8d68. Its oracle is UNCHANGED since\n    changes 1226/1227, so a green here cannot come from a weakened assertion: the cell was failing\n    because the PRODUCT was wrong, and the product is now fixed.\n\nWHEN READING THAT RUN: take the per-cell verdicts and the\n\"[jira-live-canary] collected=N executed=N skipped=0\" line, NOT the pass/fail count. Two separate\ntimes this session a raw count misled a reader of these logs — once appearing to show collection\ncollapsing from 49 cells to 9 (it was a different pytest session in the same log), and once because a\nper-test \"Captured log call\" banner uses the same underscore format as pytest's FAILURES section.\n\nNOTHING ELSE IS OUTSTANDING on this story. All six of the harness failures it originally surfaced are\nresolved: 727f and d103 (closed), b9b8, d067 (closed), the inbound-link cell (proven NOT a product\ndefect — the failing run predated b9b8's priming pass, and the skip it exposed is structural and\ncorrect by phase order), and the assignee cell (its own oracle defect, fixed, which then exposed\n8d68)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785714643240687001,"uuid":"f9a07bdf-e54e-41b4-a26d-f34144bf9700"}